          {
            "at": "tryIt",
            "caption": "Moving the combined check below the single check makes assert catch the bug.",
            "whatIf": "def fizz_buzz(n):\n    if n % 3 == 0:\n        return \"Fizz\"\n    if n % 15 == 0:\n        return \"FizzBuzz\"\n    if n % 5 == 0:\n        return \"Buzz\"\n    return str(n)\n\nprint([fizz_buzz(n) for n in range(1, 16)])\nfor n, expected in [(15, \"FizzBuzz\"), (9, \"Fizz\"), (10, \"Buzz\"), (7, \"7\")]:\n    assert fizz_buzz(n) == expected, f\"{n}: got {fizz_buzz(n)}\"\nprint(\"All my examples pass\")",
